{"base_rate":0.4296977660972405,"brier":0.11604099868593955,"bss":0.5264745895517129,"bss_hi":0.5945077932039323,"bss_lo":0.4467634333246466,"chart":{"base":[619.2,47.8],"fp":[261.3,327.7],"lead":"62,222.2 272,198.9 482,150.8 692,87.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.53 — higher than 94% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +9pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.4 °C — better than 20% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 4%; promised 93% → rained 84%"},"rel":"64.2,447.5 237.5,304 649.5,102"},"country":"CH","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.0709592641261498,"ess":368.41781173663236,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Zuerich</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Zuerich rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nZUERICH/FLUNTERN, 2.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.53, ranked 13 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(5&ndash;39) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>304</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>27%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>76%</td><td class='num'><b>66%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>241</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Zuerich</b> <span class=\"muted\">Switzerland</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.53</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>5&ndash;39\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Zuerich &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Zuerich\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.25763157894737,378.4078947368421 101.69371428571428,309.2 203.48536585365855,191.1219512195122 326.5421875,69.1875 404.4646473029046,19.510373443983383 404.4646473029046,33.103734439834 326.5421875,143.2671875 203.48536585365855,271.0243902439024 101.69371428571428,361.2 59.25763157894737,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"225.59001314060447\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"225.59001314060447\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.25763157894737,366.4342105263158 101.69371428571428,283.2 203.48536585365855,213.3170731707317 326.5421875,143.125 404.4646473029046,57.26970954356847\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 304 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.25763157894737\" cy=\"366.4342105263158\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 27% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"101.69371428571428\" cy=\"283.2\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 41%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"203.48536585365855\" cy=\"213.3170731707317\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 76%&amp;#10;It rained 66% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"326.5421875\" cy=\"143.125\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 241 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"404.4646473029046\" cy=\"57.26970954356847\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(43%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Zuerich the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.54) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.50).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>183</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.496</td><td class='num'>5.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.517</td><td class='num'>4.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.539</td><td class='num'>5.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.540</td><td class='num'>7.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":47.36667,"lon":8.55,"n":761,"n_cities":213,"name":"Zuerich","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0035526315789473684,"n":304,"obs":0.04276315789473684,"sig":true},{"hi":0.23,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.12342857142857142,"n":70,"obs":0.2714285714285714,"sig":true},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.23,"mean":0.4109756097560976,"n":82,"obs":0.4634146341463415,"sig":false},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.63,"mean":0.75859375,"n":64,"obs":0.65625,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9787136929460581,"n":241,"obs":0.8921161825726142,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.2,"provisional":false,"rank":13,"rank_hi":39.0,"rank_lo":5.0,"reliability":0.006181076061177444,"resolution":0.13426955288653064,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"zuerich","station":"ZUERICH/FLUNTERN","timezone":"Europe/Zurich"}